WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.700
Oh, hi there.
噢，嗨。

9
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.680
Should we tell everyone how we walked in today?
我们要告诉大家我们今天是怎么走进来的吗？

10
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:28.760
It was ridiculous.
太荒唐了。

11
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:30.940
It's that thing.
就是那种事。

12
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.380
I think when you're friends with someone, you start to, like, dress alike.
我觉得当你和某人成为朋友时，你们开始，比如，穿得像对方。

13
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.600
Because we both showed up with our hair in braids.
因为我们俩今天都扎着辫子来了。

14
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.240
Carrying giant boxes.
还提着巨大的盒子。

15
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.240
And then we realized they're the same exact box of iteMs.
然后我们发现那是完全一模一样的物品盒。

16
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.620
Which we'll get to later.
我们稍后会聊到这个。

17
00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.080
Yes.
没错。

18
00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.840
But you said we should title this episode Braids and Boxes.
但你说我们应该把这集标题定为“辫子与盒子”。

19
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.040
Braids and Boxes.
辫子与盒子。

20
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:50.900
Here we go.
开始了。

21
00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:56.160
The actual title of the episode that we're breaking down today is Live in the Dream Part 1.
我们今天剖析的这一集，实际标题是《活在梦中（上）》。

22
00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:02.960
It is Season 9, Episode 22, written by Nikki Schwartz-Wright and directed by Jeffrey Blitz.
这是第九季第22集，由尼基·施瓦茨-赖特编剧，杰弗里·布里茨执导。

23
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.520
Would you like a summary?
你想听听剧情摘要吗？

24
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:05.780
So much.
太想了。

25
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:06.740
All right.
好的。

26
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:12.120
In this episode, Jim is taking time off from athlete to focus on his marriage.
在这一集中，吉姆从Athlead公司请假，专注于他的婚姻。

27
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:13.780
Wow.
哇。

28
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.660
Big deal, finally.
大事，终于。

29
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.340
Andy quits Dunder Mifflin to pursue his dreaMs.
安迪从邓德·米夫林辞职去追求他的梦想。

30
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.480
He's going to be something.
他要干出一番事业。

31
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.920
He might host a food show.
他可能会主持美食节目。

32
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:24.960
He might dance.
他可能会跳舞。

33
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:25.780
He might act.
他可能会演戏。

34
00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.020
There's so many options for Andy.
安迪的选择太多了。

35
00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.040
Anything goes.
一切皆有可能。

36
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:29.960
Anything could happen.
什么事都可能发生。

37
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.920
Angela is mourning the confiscation of her cats.
安吉拉正在为她的猫被没收而哀悼。

38
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.320
All her cats get taken away in this episode.
在这一集中，她所有的猫都被带走了。

39
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.760
To Saksworth.
去了萨克斯沃斯。

40
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:40.180
I know.
我知道。

41
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.520
I remember that.
我记得那段。

42
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.360
That made me laugh.
那让我笑了。

43
00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:43.860
I know.
我知道。

44
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:49.080
And finally, Dwight is going to receive his black belt.
最后，德怀特即将获得他的黑带。

45
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.020
Finally.
终于。

46
00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.940
In the place he loves moSt.
在他最爱的地方。

47
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:52.360
Yes.
是的。

48
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:53.700
All right.
好的。

49
00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.580
To kick things off, we got a fan question from Emma L.
首先，我们收到了一位粉丝艾玛·L的提问。

50
00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.100
in Waterloo, Ontario, Canada, who said,
她来自加拿大安大略省滑铁卢，她说：

51
00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:05.500
I want to know everything about what it was like to work with Michael Imperioli as Sensei Billy.
我想了解关于迈克尔·因佩里奥利饰演比利师傅的所有幕后故事。

52
00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.920
I think his storyline and chemistry with Rainn Wilson is pure genius.
我觉得他的剧情线以及与雷恩·威尔森之间的化学反应简直是天才之作。

53
00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.500
How did he come to be cast in this role?
他是怎么得到这个角色的呢？

54
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:19.860
Well, Emma, we are very excited to let you know that we got to interview Michael Imperioli.
艾玛，我们很高兴地告诉你，我们采访到了迈克尔·因佩里奥利。

55
00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:20.520
We did.
没错。

56
00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.360
All about his time on the show.
聊了他参与这部剧的全部经历。

57
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.060
And his interview is our Fast Facts 1, 2, and 3 today.
他的采访内容就是我们今天“快速事实”1、2、3期的主题。

58
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.480
So here you go.
所以，请看。

59
00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.820
We're so thrilled to have you.
非常高兴你能来。

60
00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:32.200
Yeah.
是啊。

61
00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:32.600
Thank you.
谢谢。

62
00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:33.680
I'm glad to be here.
很高兴能来这里。

63
00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.160
It was so crazy when I was watching this episode.
我看这一集的时候觉得太不可思议了。

64
00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.680
And then all of a sudden, you popped up on my screen.
突然之间，你就出现在了我的屏幕上。

65
00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:43.880
And it was just the week before I ran into you on the street in New York.
那就在我于纽约街头偶遇你的一周之后。

66
00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.460
It was right after that.
就在那之后不久。

67
00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:45.740
Yeah.
是的。

68
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:46.920
It was pretty wild.
真是太疯狂了。

69
00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.060
It was such crazy timing.
这时间点巧得离谱。

70
00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.500
So thanks for being with us today.
所以谢谢你今天能来参加我们的节目。

71
00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.260
We'll just hop right in.
我们直接进入正题吧。

72
00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:57.040
So we always ask our guests, how did you get your job on The Office?
我们总是问嘉宾，你是怎么得到《办公室》里的角色的？

73
00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.560
Rainn told me that they Googled actors who were black belts.
雷恩告诉我，他们当时在谷歌上搜索拥有黑带段位的演员。

74
00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.960
And your name came up?
然后就搜到了你的名字？

75
00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.360
And my name was on a liSt.
我的名字就在名单上。

76
00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.600
So I don't know how many other actors they went through before they got to me who had black.
所以我不知道在联系到我之前，他们还找过多少其他拥有黑带的演员。

77
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.900
Maybe Chuck Norris and I don't know who else.
也许是查克·诺里斯之类的，我也不知道还有谁。

78
00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.200
And that was really it.
事情就是这样。

79
00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.320
And then I got the script and I thought it was really funny.
后来我拿到了剧本，觉得非常有趣。

80
00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:21.120
And I mean, the show's great and really funny.
我是说，这部剧本身就很棒，而且特别好笑。

81
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.160
And that was it.
就是这样。

82
00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.340
That was how I got it.
我就是这么得到这个角色的。

83
00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.140
Had you watched the show before?
你之前看过这部剧吗？

84
00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.920
Yeah, like everybody on the planet pretty much.
看过，几乎地球上每个人都看过吧。

85
00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.360
Yeah, I thought it was really funny.
是的，我觉得它真的很有趣。

86
00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.980
And it was really a fun sequence, you know, a fun part of the episode.
那真是一段有趣的戏份，你知道，是那一集中很有意思的部分。

87
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.260
It's just so ridiculous.
简直太荒谬了。

88
00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:43.540
It was really fun to watch it again because I hadn't seen it in quite a long time.
重温这一集真的很有趣，因为我已经很久没看了。

89
00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.640
And I was like, it's even funnier than it was when I first saw it.
我当时想，它比我第一次看的时候还要好笑。

90
00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:51.480
And when I did it, it stands up pretty well to be ridiculous and funny.
而且当我回看自己演的部分时，发现它依然非常荒谬好笑，经得起推敲。

91
00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:52.840
It really does.
确实如此。

92
00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.700
I loved Sensei Billy, like how calm he was.
我超爱比利师傅，喜欢他那种冷静的样子。

93
00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.900
And just matter of fact, when Dwight's doing all this crazy crap.
当德怀特在那儿做各种疯狂举动时，他却表现得那么一本正经。

94
00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:06.100
Well, listen, there are three scenes that you're in.
听着，你在剧中总共有三场戏。

95
00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:11.920
You know, one of them is the very first montage where Dwight's trying to kick the board, which is hilarious.
其中一场是最初的蒙太奇片段，德怀特试图踢碎木板，那段真是太搞笑了。

96
00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:15.840
Did you give Rain any tips or did he just like go for it?
你有给雷恩什么建议吗，还是他直接就上手了？

97
00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.580
No, he just went for it.
没有，他直接就上了。

98
00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:27.580
You know, I've done Korean martial arts, mostly taekwondo for like 22 years.
你知道，我练过韩国武术，主要是跆拳道，练了大概22年。

99
00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.480
And sometimes you do break boards, you know, that's part of it.
有时候确实需要踢碎木板，那是练习的一部分。

100
00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:41.100
Like usually on a test, when you're going up a level or something, you do that as a, you know, you're testing your kind of accuracy and speed and things like that.
通常在晋级考试之类的场合，你会通过这种方式来测试自己的精准度、速度以及诸如此类的能力。

101
00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:48.200
And I've never gotten kicked in the balls doing that, but I've held boards for other people, testing, especially for kids.
我做那个动作时从来没被踢到过裆部，但我帮别人拿过木板，做测试的时候，尤其是给小孩子拿。

102
00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.000
Kids aren't as accurate as adults sometimes.
小孩子有时候没那么准。

103
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.500
And they'll kick your hands and, you know, holding boards for people.
他们会踢到你的手，你知道的，帮人拿木板就是这样。

104
00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:57.320
I've gotten my hands pretty banged up.
我的手被伤得够呛。

105
00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.220
So that's kind of accurate.
所以那确实挺准的。

106
00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.300
That really happens.
那是真的会发生。

107
00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.460
But he just went for it.
但他就是直接上了。

108
00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:07.060
You know, I don't remember if he told me that he trained or not.
你知道，我不记得他有没有跟我说他练过。

109
00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.440
I'm pretty sure he had not trained.
我很确定他没练过。

110
00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.100
He had not trained, yeah.
他没练过，没错。

111
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.080
It didn't seem like he did.
看起来也不像练过。

112
00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.800
But he just went for it.
但他就是直接上了。

113
00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.220
And, I mean, it's just so silly and fun.
而且，我是说，这真的太傻太好玩了。

114
00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:21.840
It's so silly.
太傻了。

115
00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:28.000
And then the next one is the belt ceremony in the office, the place he loves the most, right?
接下来就是办公室里的腰带授予仪式，他最喜欢的地方，对吧？

116
00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.560
And then you couldn't get the belt off him and he's kind of awkwardly thrusting at you.
然后你没法把腰带从他身上解下来，他还在那儿笨拙地对着你挺胯。

117
00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:36.680
And you're so, since I'm Billy, she's like, this isn't going to work.
而你，因为我是比利，她就觉得，这可不行。

118
00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:37.260
Okay.
好吧。

119
00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.920
He's trying his best to keep composure because that's what a martial artist does, right?
他正努力保持镇定，因为那是武术家该做的，对吧？

120
00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:45.000
He's, you know, he doesn't let his anger get the best of him.
他，你知道，他不会让愤怒冲昏头脑。

121
00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:52.420
But, you know, in martial arts, a lot of the movements, most of them really come from the hips, from the center of the body.
但是，你知道，在武术中，很多动作，大部分确实来自髋部，来自身体中心。

122
00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.800
You know, that's really where you get your power if you're throwing a punch.
你知道，如果你要出拳，力量确实就是从那儿来的。

123
00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:02.700
You know, if you watch like athletes like golfers or baseball players or tennis players, you can see it.
你知道，如果你观察像高尔夫球手、棒球运动员或网球运动员这样的运动员，你就能看出来。

124
00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.580
Like those, yeah, those motions with the arMs.
就像那些，没错，那些手臂的动作。

125
00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:06.520
Yeah.
没错。

126
00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.780
I have a really good forehand.
我的正手击球非常棒。

127
00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:13.100
I don't want to brag, but I have a really, well, now I'm bragging, but I have a really good forehand at tennis.
我不想吹牛，但我确实，好吧，现在我是在吹牛了，但我的网球正手真的很厉害。

128
00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:18.900
And I'm short and people don't expect it because it's all in that twist, that torque from your hips.
我个子不高，人们对此没抱太大期望，因为关键全在于那种扭转，那种来自髋部的扭矩。

129
00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:24.220
So a lot of the movements in martial arts come from the hips, like punches and blocks and kicks even, right?
所以武术中的很多动作都来自髋部，比如出拳、格挡，甚至踢腿，对吧？

130
00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:29.380
So I think that's what he was, he was figuring, I have to use my hips here.
所以我认为他当时就是这么想的，我得在这儿用上我的髋部。

131
00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:34.500
You know, even getting the belt, like everything we do comes from the hips and it wasn't necessary.
你知道，甚至连拿腰带也是，我们做的每件事都来自髋部，虽然没必要。

132
00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.100
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

133
00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:36.860
That's my theory, at leaSt.
至少这是我的理论。

134
00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:40.820
Do you remember like breaking it all in that scene?
你还记得那场戏里大家都笑场了吗？

135
00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:52.100
Because I remember watching it and I, I think there's no shots of me in this sequence because they had to avoid me because I couldn't keep it together.
因为我记得看那段的时候，我想这段戏里没有我的镜头，因为他们得避开我，我当时根本憋不住笑。

136
00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.940
No, I lost it a few times.
不，我笑场了好几次。

137
00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:58.240
It was just so, you know, he's just so committed, you know.
实在是太，你知道，他当时太投入了，你知道的。

138
00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:03.940
Fans wrote in and pointed out every time someone broke and it's, we're all, they clocked everybody.
粉丝们写信指出每次有人笑场的情况，我们所有人都被他们盯上了。

139
00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.260
Except you.
除了你。

140
00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:10.260
My memory, Michael, is that you were very good at keeping it together.
迈克尔，我的记忆是，你非常擅长憋笑。

141
00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.260
Are you an actor that breaks a lot?
你是个容易笑场的演员吗？

142
00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:14.420
Because I was so impressed.
因为我当时印象非常深刻。

143
00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.940
If it's really funny.
如果真的很好笑的话。

144
00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:17.640
Yeah.
是的。

145
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:18.440
Sometimes.
有时候吧。

146
00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:30.100
You know, on The Sopranos, the time everybody broke was when it was the mother, Livia's post-funeral gathering at The Soprano House.
你知道，在《黑道家族》里，大家全都笑场的那次，是在利维亚的葬礼后，在黑道家族的房子里聚会的时候。

147
00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:34.480
And everybody's there, the whole family and all the gangsters and all the friends of the family.
每个人都在那儿，整个家族，所有的黑帮成员，还有所有家族的朋友。

148
00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:41.920
They're talking about this woman that everybody hated, really, and who hated everybody, trying to find nice things to say.
他们在谈论这个大家其实都很讨厌的女人，而她也讨厌所有人，大家都在努力找些好话来说。

149
00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:49.020
And then they play her favorite song, which was this really schmaltzy love song from Carousel sung in this very high-pitched voice.
然后他们放了她最喜欢的歌，那是《旋转木马》里的一首非常煽情的爱情歌曲，用那种很尖的嗓音唱出来的。

150
00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:53.080
And when they put that song on, everybody just lost it.
当他们放那首歌的时候，所有人都彻底破功了。

151
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.220
And they tried to do it again.
他们又试了一次。

152
00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:58.560
And every time that song came on, everybody just lost it.
每次那首歌一响，大家就彻底失控了。

153
00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.740
And then they realized, well, we can't play the song.
后来他们意识到，好吧，我们不能放这首歌。

154
00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.980
So let's just pretend we're listening to it.
所以我们假装在听就好了。

155
00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.060
And that still didn't work.
结果还是不行。

156
00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.640
To the point where the director started yelling at people.
以至于导演开始对大家大吼大叫。

157
00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:10.260
It was totally out of character for him because he had directed a lot of our episodes.
这完全不像他平时的作风，因为他执导过我们很多集。

158
00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.020
And he was a sweetheart.
他本来是个大好人。

159
00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:18.160
But he just couldn't do the scene because we were just, it just became this thing that was just too ridiculous.
但他就是拍不了那场戏，因为我们当时的状态实在太荒唐了。

160
00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:20.680
It's hard to come back from that, too.
那种状态也很难恢复过来。

161
00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:23.600
When you're gone, you know, when you're in that kind of laughter fit.
当你陷入那种狂笑不止的状态时，你知道的。

162
00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:23.880
No, you can't.
不，你根本停不下来。

163
00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:25.360
It's so hard to come back.
真的很难恢复。

164
00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:26.360
Yeah, you have to stop.
是啊，你必须停下来。

165
00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:28.120
You have to, you need some time.
你必须得停，你需要一点时间。

166
00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:30.100
You know, the Brits call that corpsing.
你知道吗，英国人把这叫做“尸体化”。

167
00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:31.300
You know that, right?
你知道这个词吧？

168
00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.700
I did not know that.
我不知道。

169
00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:33.560
That's what they call it.
他们就是这么叫的。

170
00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:34.660
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊，是啊。

171
00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:35.500
Because you're just dead.
因为你就像死了一样（僵住了）。

172
00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:40.700
They call it corpsing when you just can't stop laughing, which is a weird expression, right?
他们把这种无法停止大笑的状态称为“尸体化”，这说法挺奇怪的，对吧？

173
00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:41.560
It is.
确实。

174
00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:42.640
But I love it.
但我很喜欢这个词。

175
00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:47.020
That happened to Jenna and I when I had to tell her that Dwight put sprinkles in my freezer.
我和珍娜拍那场戏时就发生了这种情况，当时我得告诉她德怀特把“洒洒”放进了我的冷冻柜里。

176
00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:51.560
And I had to ask her if Roy had ever mercy killed one of her pets.
我还得问她罗伊有没有对她的宠物实施过安乐死。

177
00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:52.380
We couldn't.
我们根本拍不下去。

178
00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:53.540
Every time.
每次都笑场。

179
00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:55.140
They had to go to lunch.
他们只好让我们去吃午饭。

180
00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.940
I said, like, the cat had clawed the peas, like, the bag of peas because the cat was trying to get out of the freezer.
我说那只猫抓破了豌豆袋，因为猫想从冷冻柜里逃出来。

181
00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.640
They broke us for lunch.
他们不得不让我们中场休息去吃午饭。

182
00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:01.740
They were like, you're gone.
他们说，你们彻底没救了。

183
00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:02.700
You're corpsing.
你们“尸体化”了。

184
00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:03.420
You need time.
你们需要时间。

185
00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:04.120
Forget it.
算了吧。

186
00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:09.440
Yeah, because at that point, everything's going to be funny no matter how, you know, how you approach it.
是啊，因为到了那个地步，无论你怎么处理，一切都会变得很好笑。

187
00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.180
And it's infectious and it's uncontrollable.
而且这种情绪会传染，根本控制不住。

188
00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:13.360
It's an interesting phenomenon.
这是一种有趣的现象。

189
00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:20.120
And you can't really explain it to anyone unless you're really, because you're acting, you're not supposed to laugh, right?
你很难向别人解释，除非你亲身经历，因为你在演戏，你不应该笑，对吧？

190
00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.580
Which makes it worse, I think.
我觉得这反而让情况更糟了。

191
00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:23.440
Makes it worse, yeah.
确实更糟了。

192
00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.780
It's like, don't think of the word elephant or something.
就像那种“别去想大象”之类的心理暗示。

193
00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:27.580
It's kind of like that.
差不多就是那样。

194
00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:35.400
Well, speaking of laughing, after the belt thrusting, we get to Dwight's demonstration.
说到笑，在腰带猛冲动作之后，就到了德怀特的演示环节。

195
00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:36.200
Yeah.
没错。

196
00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.560
Which is so incredible.
那场戏太精彩了。

197
00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:46.460
I have to ask, with all of your experience, is anything he's doing in this scene accurate in any way?
我得问问，以你的经验，他在那场戏里做的动作有任何准确的地方吗？

198
00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:49.300
Is he doing any actual moves here?
他做的那些动作有实际意义吗？

199
00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:57.900
You know, some of the basic techniques he's executing, but he doesn't really know how to do them properly.
你知道，他用了一些基本技巧，但他其实并不知道怎么正确地做出来。

200
00:09:58.500 --> 00:09:58.740
Okay.
好吧。

201
00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:07.300
Is Sensei Billy giving him a black belt, like, sort of patronizingly?
比利老师给他黑带，是不是有点居高临下的意思？

202
00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.820
Has he earned his black belt, in your opinion?
在你看来，他拿到黑带是实至名归吗？

203
00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:10.720
I think he's earned it.
我觉得他是实至名归的。

204
00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:13.740
Well, he said he's one of the most tenacious people he's ever seen.
嗯，他说过这是他见过最坚韧的人之一。

205
00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.240
So, I think that tenaciousness.
所以，我觉得那种坚韧劲儿。

206
00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:26.360
You know, a black belt in martial arts, you have to remember, is you're not competing or comparing your level of skill and your development to anyone else.
你要知道，武术里的黑带，你得记住，它不是让你去和别人竞争，也不是让你拿自己的技术水平和成长进度去跟别人比。

207
00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:27.700
It's about your progression.
它关乎的是你自己的进步。

208
00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:36.660
So, you can have a black belt, two black belts that have trained the same amount of time, and one's a super great athlete, and one's not.
所以，你可以有两个都练了同样长时间的黑带选手，其中一个运动天赋超群，另一个则不然。

209
00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:45.660
And they're going to be very different martial artists, you know, because natural athleticism and stuff, you know, I mean, I'm 58.
他们会成为非常不同的武术家，因为天生的运动能力之类的因素，你知道，毕竟我都58岁了。

210
00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.660
I still train.
我还在训练。

211
00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:52.540
But, you know, you see some of these kids at 25 doing stuff that's just incredible that I'm not going to do.
但是，你会看到一些25岁的年轻人做出的动作简直不可思议，我是做不到了。

212
00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:57.700
I mean, I have basic techniques that I've worked on for many years that I'm comfortable with.
我的意思是，我有一些练了很多年的基本功，我对此感到很自在。

213
00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.020
I like the fitness of it.
我喜欢这种健身方式。

214
00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:04.840
But even the belt levels and that kind of thing is about your own progress and what you've done.
但即便是腰带等级之类的东西，也都是关于你自己的进步和你所付出的努力。

215
00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:13.720
So, I guess Sensi Billy, I love that we're talking about this, like, Sensi Billy said he's very tenacious and he trained with someone for 20 years who ripped him off, right?
所以，我想比利老师——我很高兴我们在讨论这个——比利老师说他非常坚韧，而且他曾跟一个骗了他的人练了20年，对吧？

216
00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:14.380
Yeah.
是的。

217
00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:23.780
Yeah.
没错。

218
00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:28.840
You know, it's a great legitimate form of art or fitness and training and all those things.
你知道，这是一种非常正统的艺术形式，或者说健身和训练方式，诸如此类。

219
00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:34.480
You know, and I've seen people who were black belts who had zero athleticism,
你知道，我见过一些毫无运动天赋的黑带选手，

220
00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:45.040
but they worked really hard and they did have their basic techniques and they were able to kind of fulfill the requirements that the different levels offered, you know?
但他们工作非常努力，掌握了基本功，并且能够达到不同等级所要求的标准，你明白吗？

221
00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.400
So, it's really about your own progress.
所以，这真的关乎你自己的进步。

222
00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:56.260
I think that's really beautiful and it's also making me feel like maybe I could be a black belt if it really is about me.
我觉得这真的很美妙，也让我觉得如果这真的是关于我自己的话，也许我也能拿到黑带。

223
00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.480
Like, if I really took this seriously.
比如，如果我真的认真对待这件事的话。

224
00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.200
And you put the time in.
而且你投入了时间。

225
00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:11.540
Yes, like, truly inspired by this idea of this journey, of this physical, mental, spiritual journey, committing to this thing.
是的，真的被这种旅程的理念所激励，这种身体、心理和精神上的旅程，全身心地投入其中。

226
00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:12.200
Yeah.
没错。

227
00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:17.460
That is, like, so beautiful that this is open to all people.
这种对所有人开放的理念，真是太美好了。

228
00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:18.160
Yeah.
是啊。

229
00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:21.180
I did not know that and I absolutely love it.
我之前不知道这一点，我真的太喜欢了。

230
00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:32.360
Yeah, you know, my main teacher, Grandmaster Taesun Kang, has been teaching for, I think it's over 40 years and he's dedicated his life to this, right?
是啊，你知道，我的主教练姜泰善大师，教拳已经有，我想超过40年了，他把一生都奉献给了这项事业，对吧？

231
00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:35.680
He just got inducted into the Taekwondo Hall of Fame, right?
他刚入选了跆拳道名人堂，对吧？

232
00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.480
This lifetime achievement.
这是终身成就。

233
00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:41.240
But he has a lot of students that have been with him for many, many, many years.
但他有很多学生跟了他很多、很多、很多年。

234
00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:48.640
And this last test, they have a black belt test twice a year and he has a couple of schools in the New York area.
在最近的一次测试中——他们一年有两次黑带测试，他在纽约地区有几家道馆。

235
00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:55.480
The last test, three women all over 50 got fourth degree black belts.
上次测试，三位50多岁的女性拿到了黑带四段。

236
00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.500
That's amazing.
那太了不起了。

237
00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:57.240
That's awesome.
太棒了。

238
00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:05.480
The highest testers of that batch, that was last November, December, were three women over 50, close to 60.
那批测试者中成绩最好的，那是去年十一、十二月的事了，是三位50多岁、快60岁的女性。

239
00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:06.280
Wow.
哇。

240
00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:11.740
Well, as a woman who just turned 50 this year, I just think that's so beautiful.
作为一个今年刚满50岁的女性，我觉得这真是太美好了。

241
00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:12.700
Yeah.
是啊。

242
00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:18.500
It was really cool to see that last winner, those three women get, you know, as the highest testers and get all getting
看到上次那三位女性作为成绩最好的测试者，拿到黑带四段，真的很酷，

243
00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:25.240
fourth degree black belts, which means they've all been training, you know, 20 years, maybe 20 plus years.
这意味着她们都已经训练了，你知道，20年，可能20多年了。

244
00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:25.880
Wow.
哇。

245
00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:26.760
That's so cool.
太酷了。

246
00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:28.180
That inspires me.
这激励了我。

247
00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:32.720
My sister-in-law, who's around our age, Jenna, got her black belt this week.
我的嫂子珍娜，和我们年纪差不多，这周也拿到了黑带。

248
00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.500
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

249
00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:35.780
And I'm so proud of her.
我真为她感到骄傲。

250
00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.820
She's in Colorado, but she's been studying a long time.
她在科罗拉多州，但她已经学习了很长时间了。

251
00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:43.400
And so it was just sort of really cool that we were talking to you today and Sensei Billy and all of that.
所以今天能和你以及比利老师（Sensei Billy）聊聊，感觉真的很棒。

252
00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:45.460
So I told her, I was like, way to go, girl.
所以我告诉她，我说，干得漂亮，姑娘。

253
00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:46.360
Yeah.
没错。

254
00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.360
It's a really great way to stay fit.
这确实是一种保持健康的好方法。

255
00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:52.840
You know, for me, when I started, I was really out of shape.
你知道，对我来说，刚开始的时候，我的状态真的很差。

256
00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:54.300
I was smoking cigarettes.
那时我抽烟。

257
00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:57.360
I was drinking and I wasn't exercising at all.
我喝酒，而且完全不锻炼。

258
00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:02.000
And my kids started going and I would go pick them up and watch and stuff.
后来我的孩子们开始去练习，我就去接他们，顺便看看之类的。

259
00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.700
And then I, you know, this is 22 years ago.
然后，你知道，那是22年前的事了。

260
00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:09.760
And then slowly I started and I eventually realized I can either, I had to choose one,
后来我慢慢开始尝试，最终我意识到我只能二选一，我必须做出选择，

261
00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:14.340
smoking cigarettes or doing Taekwondo because they didn't, they didn't go together.
要么抽烟，要么练跆拳道，因为这两者根本没法共存。

262
00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.740
And, you know, it started me on a path of health.
你知道，这让我走上了一条健康之路。

263
00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:24.280
There's a humility to it and the thing of respect and thing about meeting goals and
它有一种谦逊的特质，还有关于尊重、实现目标以及

264
00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.120
exceeding goals and challenging yourself.
超越目标和挑战自我的精神。

265
00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:33.240
And what I liked, I always had problems committing to a gym program because I would get bored doing,
我喜欢的一点是，我以前总没法坚持去健身房，因为我觉得做那些

266
00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:35.540
you know, like weight machines and things like that.
你知道，像器械训练之类的东西很无聊。

267
00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:40.940
This is about learning a skill, you know, and for that hour that you're doing a class,
而这关乎学习一项技能，你知道，在上课的那一小时里，

268
00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.360
you can't think about anything else.
你根本没法想别的事情。

269
00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:46.440
It's not like you're on a treadmill watching CNN or, you know, list, you know, checking emails.
这不像你在跑步机上看着CNN，或者，你知道，听着什么，或者查收邮件。

270
00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:50.880
You can't really think of anything else except what you're doing in the moment because
你真的没法想别的事，只能专注于当下正在做的事情，因为

271
00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.560
it takes all that concentration.
这需要全神贯注。

272
00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:53.800
That was really helpful for me.
这对我有很大帮助。

273
00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:54.880
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

274
00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.640
I feel the same way on a tennis court.
我在网球场上也有同感。

275
00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.820
You can't think it, you can't, you don't have your phone.
你没法分心，你不能，你也没法看手机。

276
00:14:58.940 --> 00:14:59.400
You can't think of it.
你根本没法去想别的事。

277
00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:02.080
I take my watch off because I don't want it buzzing or anything.
我会把手表摘下来，因为我不想让它震动或者发出什么声音。

278
00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:02.600
Yeah.
没错。

279
00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:03.280
Yeah.
是啊。

280
00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:04.000
That's great.
那太棒了。

281
00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:06.240
Well, Michael, do you have any memories?
那么，迈克尔，你有什么回忆吗？

282
00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:10.420
I know you were only on set that one time, but do you have any memories from being on
我知道你只去过片场一次，但对于当时和我们一起在

283
00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:13.400
