Fan question from Jenna F.
来自洛杉矶的珍娜·F的粉丝提问。

936
00:41:58.290 --> 00:41:59.110
in Los Angeles.
在洛杉矶的。

937
00:41:59.390 --> 00:42:00.210
Oh, Jenna F.
哦，珍娜·F。

938
00:42:00.250 --> 00:42:00.590
wrote in?
写信进来的？

939
00:42:00.690 --> 00:42:01.250
She did.
是的。

940
00:42:01.250 --> 00:42:12.450
She noticed that in this very quick little moment, this little B-roll under David Wallace's talking head, that we see a shot of Andy at this color printer,
她注意到在大卫·华莱士采访镜头下的那个非常短的空镜里，我们看到了安迪在用那台彩色打印机，

941
00:42:12.730 --> 00:42:16.370
and he is holding his headshot composite.
手里还拿着他的头像照组合图。

942
00:42:17.050 --> 00:42:17.290
Yes.
没错。

943
00:42:17.670 --> 00:42:18.250
Jenna F.
珍娜·F。

944
00:42:18.430 --> 00:42:21.830
said, this is my favorite comedic prop from the whole show.
说，这是整部剧里她最喜欢的喜剧道具。

945
00:42:22.030 --> 00:42:24.870
I literally spit out my coffee when I saw it.
我看到的时候真的把咖啡喷出来了。

946
00:42:25.110 --> 00:42:27.490
Please tell me everything about this prop.
请告诉我关于这个道具的一切。

947
00:42:31.050 --> 00:42:32.230
It's just brilliant.
简直太天才了。

948
00:42:32.590 --> 00:42:35.870
I mean, I truly did spit out my coffee when I saw it.
我是说，我看到的时候确实把咖啡喷出来了。

949
00:42:35.970 --> 00:42:38.310
I was taking a sip of coffee, and I choked on it.
我当时正喝着咖啡，结果被呛到了。

950
00:42:38.670 --> 00:42:40.750
It is so perfect to me.
我觉得它简直太完美了。

951
00:42:41.130 --> 00:42:44.110
I reached out to Ed, because I had to ask him about this.
我联系了埃德，因为我必须就这件事问问他。

952
00:42:44.170 --> 00:42:47.870
He clearly had to take all these pictures of all these different characters.
他显然得拍下所有这些不同角色的照片。

953
00:42:48.750 --> 00:42:50.030
Here's what Ed had to say.
以下是埃德的说法。

954
00:42:50.590 --> 00:42:51.490
Hey, Jenna.
嘿，珍娜。

955
00:42:51.490 --> 00:42:54.050
Jenna, I saw your text.
珍娜，我看到你的短信了。

956
00:42:55.430 --> 00:43:01.870
I don't remember a lot of details about that composite headshot, but I agree.
关于那张合成头像照，我不记得太多细节了，但我同意你的看法。

957
00:43:01.870 --> 00:43:03.550
It is really damn funny.
它确实非常搞笑。

958
00:43:03.550 --> 00:43:17.570
And I just remember we wanted to kind of, I don't know, nod to what it's like to be starting out as an actor, and especially a comedy actor.
我只记得我们当时想，怎么说呢，向刚入行的演员，尤其是喜剧演员的经历致敬。

959
00:43:17.570 --> 00:43:23.010
And I don't know about you, but I definitely had a composite headshot like that with a bunch of different characters.
我不知道你怎么样，但我绝对也拍过那种包含各种角色的合成头像照。

960
00:43:23.670 --> 00:43:33.290
When you're starting out, it's sort of what you think the casting business wants from you, which is like a lot of options and a lot of variety.
刚入行时，你总觉得选角行业需要你提供很多选择和多样性。

961
00:43:34.370 --> 00:43:40.790
And sometimes we try a little too hard when we put those headshots together.
有时候我们在制作这些头像照时确实用力过猛了。

962
00:43:41.270 --> 00:43:46.610
I don't even know if young actors today even do headshots.
我甚至不知道现在的年轻演员是否还会拍这种头像照。

963
00:43:47.050 --> 00:43:48.750
Everything's so online these days.
如今一切都在线上了。

964
00:43:49.030 --> 00:43:52.050
But it was definitely a fun nod.
但这绝对是一个有趣的致敬。

965
00:43:52.290 --> 00:43:57.390
And I remember brainstorming like, well, okay, if we're doing a composite headshot, like, what are the different characters?
我记得当时我们集思广益，心想，好吧，如果我们要拍一张合成头像照，那应该包含哪些不同的角色呢？

966
00:43:58.990 --> 00:44:02.890
And so we just tried to come up with a good variety.
于是我们试着构思了各种各样的角色。

967
00:44:02.890 --> 00:44:06.550
And, of course, there's always like a nerd character, a jock.
当然，总少不了书呆子、运动健将之类的角色。

968
00:44:07.730 --> 00:44:10.110
And then what else did we do in that?
那里面还有什么角色来着？

969
00:44:10.190 --> 00:44:10.810
A judge.
法官。

970
00:44:11.030 --> 00:44:13.910
And then there's just like the cool guy right in the middle.
中间还有一个酷哥。

971
00:44:14.230 --> 00:44:23.790
So, yeah, it's just a nod to classic, you know, actors starting out trying to get that headshot to get those parts.
所以，没错，这只是向那些刚入行、为了争取角色而努力拍摄头像照的经典演员们致敬。

972
00:44:24.290 --> 00:44:26.010
I guess that's what it is.
我想就是这样吧。

973
00:44:26.990 --> 00:44:27.990
I just love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

974
00:44:28.150 --> 00:44:29.330
It is so true.
真是太真实了。

975
00:44:29.910 --> 00:44:31.090
We all did it.
我们都干过这事。

976
00:44:31.410 --> 00:44:40.270
In honor of Andy's composite headshots, I went through my drawer and I have brought in my first headshots.
为了向安迪的合成头像照致敬，我翻了翻抽屉，带了我最早的几张头像照过来。

977
00:44:40.450 --> 00:44:42.490
And then Jenna told me to do the same.
然后珍娜也让我这么做。

978
00:44:42.730 --> 00:44:44.570
So we're going to have a show and tell.
所以我们要来一场展示分享会。

979
00:44:44.750 --> 00:44:45.410
We are.
没错。

980
00:44:46.030 --> 00:44:51.130
So my very first headshot was – Cassie has stood up to see this.
我最早的一张头像照是——卡西站起来看了。

981
00:44:51.270 --> 00:44:52.150
People are standing up.
大家都站起来了。

982
00:44:52.330 --> 00:44:52.390
Okay.
好吧。

983
00:44:52.670 --> 00:44:52.910
Okay.
好吧。

984
00:44:53.430 --> 00:44:54.710
I mean, I have a stack.
我是说，我有一大叠。

985
00:44:54.710 --> 00:44:55.610
I only brought two.
我只带了两张。

986
00:44:55.730 --> 00:44:56.650
Did you bring them all?
你把所有的都带来了吗？

987
00:44:56.810 --> 00:44:57.730
No, I brought three.
没有，我带了三张。

988
00:44:57.970 --> 00:44:58.190
Okay.
好吧。

989
00:44:58.190 --> 00:45:05.490
My very first headshot, which I did not bring, was actually taken by my tech theater teacher in college.
我最早的一张头像照，我没带过来，其实是我大学的舞台技术老师拍的。

990
00:45:05.490 --> 00:45:07.410
His name is Ron Rybkowski.
他叫罗恩·雷布科夫斯基。

991
00:45:07.670 --> 00:45:08.650
I love this man.
我爱死这个人了。

992
00:45:08.850 --> 00:45:15.230
And something he did for any actor who needed it is he brought his camera in and he set up, you know, a backdrop.
他为任何有需要的演员做的一件事就是，他会带上相机，架起背景布。

993
00:45:15.230 --> 00:45:22.190
And he took a picture for each of us when we graduated for free so that we would have something when we went out to become actors.
我们毕业时，他会免费为我们每人拍一张照片，这样我们去当演员时就有照片可用了。

994
00:45:22.850 --> 00:45:24.210
It was a great picture.
那是一张很棒的照片。

995
00:45:24.670 --> 00:45:26.690
It got me in the door a lot of places.
它让我敲开了许多地方的大门。

996
00:45:27.530 --> 00:45:29.550
But, of course, I get to L.A.
但当然，我到了洛杉矶之后。

997
00:45:29.930 --> 00:45:32.430
and I get in my head about it.
我就开始钻牛角尖了。

998
00:45:32.490 --> 00:45:34.890
And I think I need to hire one of these L.A.
我觉得我得雇一位洛杉矶的专业头像摄影师来给我拍照。

999
00:45:34.990 --> 00:45:36.790
headshot photographers to take my picture.
来拍我的照片。

1000
00:45:37.030 --> 00:45:37.170
Yeah.
没错。

1001
00:45:37.530 --> 00:45:41.230
The big thing you ask yourself is what do I wear in this headshot?
你问自己的头等大事就是：拍这张定妆照我该穿什么？

1002
00:45:41.470 --> 00:45:42.090
What do I wear?
我该穿什么？

1003
00:45:42.090 --> 00:45:47.830
The advice I got was just wear something you're comfortable in, something that you're going to be able to be yourself in.
我得到的建议是，穿让你感到舒服的衣服，穿上它能让你展现真实的自我。

1004
00:45:48.110 --> 00:45:56.170
So I wore my favorite outfit, which was, at the time, a pair of brown corduroy overalls and Doc Martens.
所以我穿了我最喜欢的行头，当时是一条棕色灯芯绒背带裤，搭配马丁靴。

1005
00:45:56.270 --> 00:45:59.510
And here is my first Los Angeles headshot.
这就是我在洛杉矶拍的第一张定妆照。

1006
00:45:59.770 --> 00:46:00.950
How cute are you?
你当时多可爱啊？

1007
00:46:00.950 --> 00:46:02.110
You're so cute.
你太可爱了。

1008
00:46:02.970 --> 00:46:03.430
Okay.
好吧。

1009
00:46:03.630 --> 00:46:08.070
This headshot is super cute, but it didn't help me get many auditions.
这张定妆照超级可爱，但它没帮我争取到多少试镜机会。

1010
00:46:08.190 --> 00:46:08.470
Okay.
好吧。

1011
00:46:08.470 --> 00:46:12.990
I got some notes from agents saying, you're kind of sitting in kind of a closed-off way.
经纪人给我提了一些意见，说我坐姿看起来有点封闭。

1012
00:46:13.110 --> 00:46:14.310
You're kind of hugging your knees.
你有点像是在抱着膝盖。

1013
00:46:14.930 --> 00:46:17.670
Let's try to be maybe more open.
我们试着开放一点吧。

1014
00:46:17.910 --> 00:46:19.270
Why don't you try again?
你为什么不重拍一次呢？

1015
00:46:19.510 --> 00:46:21.970
So my hair had grown out a little bit.
于是我的头发长长了一点。

1016
00:46:21.970 --> 00:46:22.930
It was a little longer.
稍微长了一点点。

1017
00:46:23.190 --> 00:46:27.490
So I hired a new photographer, and I thought, let's do this again.
所以我雇了一位新摄影师，我想，再试一次吧。

1018
00:46:27.670 --> 00:46:27.950
Okay.
好吧。

1019
00:46:28.630 --> 00:46:30.130
You might ask yourself.
你可能会问自己。

1020
00:46:30.930 --> 00:46:32.290
Did you change your outfit?
你换衣服了吗？

1021
00:46:32.530 --> 00:46:33.070
Did not.
没换。

1022
00:46:35.030 --> 00:46:37.690
Did not sit in a less closed-off way.
坐姿也没有变得更开放。

1023
00:46:37.750 --> 00:46:39.650
You're doing the same pose, basically.
你基本上还是在摆同一个姿势。

1024
00:46:40.170 --> 00:46:44.570
Same pose, same outfit, slightly longer hair.
同样的姿势，同样的衣服，头发稍微长了一点。

1025
00:46:44.790 --> 00:46:45.810
That's all that's happened.
这就是全部的变化。

1026
00:46:45.970 --> 00:46:46.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1027
00:46:46.450 --> 00:46:47.070
That's it.
就是这样。

1028
00:46:47.970 --> 00:46:50.110
I was like, I'm going to get this right.
我当时心想，我一定要把它拍好。

1029
00:46:51.190 --> 00:46:56.070
I cut my hair again, and I was like, I'm not going to make this mistake again.
我又剪了头发，心想，我绝不会再犯同样的错误了。

1030
00:46:56.070 --> 00:46:56.590
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1031
00:46:56.910 --> 00:47:03.910
Third session, didn't end up using this one, but did have it blown up into an 8x10.
第三次拍摄，虽然最后没用这张，但我还是把它放大洗成了8x10英寸的照片。

1032
00:47:04.810 --> 00:47:05.290
Why?
为什么？

1033
00:47:06.650 --> 00:47:08.570
Why am I sitting on a stool like this?
我为什么会像这样坐在凳子上？

1034
00:47:08.590 --> 00:47:09.450
It's so weird.
太奇怪了。

1035
00:47:09.450 --> 00:47:10.690
It's so awkward.
太尴尬了。

1036
00:47:11.010 --> 00:47:12.310
It's so awkward.
太尴尬了。

1037
00:47:12.530 --> 00:47:15.430
Why is my zip-down sweater tucked into my jeans?
为什么我的拉链毛衣要塞进牛仔裤里？

1038
00:47:15.450 --> 00:47:16.250
I don't know.
我不知道。

1039
00:47:16.350 --> 00:47:17.090
What's happening?
这到底是怎么回事？

1040
00:47:17.390 --> 00:47:17.930
With a belt.
还系了条腰带。

1041
00:47:18.070 --> 00:47:23.610
She took a hoodie, a zipper sweater, she tucked it in jeans with a belt, and then straddled
她拿了一件连帽衫，一件拉链毛衣，把它塞进牛仔裤里，系上腰带，然后跨坐在

1042
00:47:23.610 --> 00:47:24.090
a stool.
凳子上。

1043
00:47:24.090 --> 00:47:25.810
It's so awkward.
太尴尬了。

1044
00:47:26.050 --> 00:47:26.770
It's awful.
太糟糕了。

1045
00:47:26.830 --> 00:47:28.990
Oh, I have so many awkward ones, too.
噢，我还有好多尴尬的照片呢。

1046
00:47:29.230 --> 00:47:35.370
There are many more before I got it right, and I actually have a whole chapter about it
在我拍出满意的照片之前，还有很多这样的作品，我其实在我的书《演员的生活》里专门写了一章

1047
00:47:35.370 --> 00:47:39.450
in my book, The Actor's Life, and you can see them all, but I'll share these online.
来讲述这段经历，你们可以看到所有的照片，但我会把这些分享到网上。

1048
00:47:40.010 --> 00:47:40.450
Okay.
好吧。

1049
00:47:40.770 --> 00:47:42.010
Well, because-
嗯，因为——

1050
00:47:42.010 --> 00:47:43.250
But it got worse before it got back.
但在好转之前，情况变得更糟了。

1051
00:47:43.550 --> 00:47:44.070
Yeah, same here.
是啊，我也是。

1052
00:47:44.270 --> 00:47:47.310
Because you told me you were bringing yours in, I was like, okay.
因为你跟我说你要带你的过来，我就想，好吧。

1053
00:47:48.690 --> 00:47:51.630
I was in New York in my early 20s.
我二十出头的时候在纽约。

1054
00:47:51.770 --> 00:47:53.970
This is when I was interning on the Conan O'Brien show.
那时候我正在柯南·奥布莱恩秀实习。

1055
00:47:54.090 --> 00:47:55.250
And I was taking acting classes.
我还在上表演课。

1056
00:47:55.770 --> 00:47:59.290
And I was going to move to LA, and one of the gals was like, you have to have a head
我当时打算搬去洛杉矶，其中一个姑娘就说，如果你要搬去洛杉矶，

1057
00:47:59.290 --> 00:48:00.870
shot if you're moving to Los Angeles.
你得准备一张头像照。

1058
00:48:01.110 --> 00:48:01.330
That's right.
没错。

1059
00:48:01.470 --> 00:48:02.090
I was like, okay.
我就想，好吧。

1060
00:48:02.930 --> 00:48:04.650
So I was like, what do I wear?
于是我问，我该穿什么呢？

1061
00:48:04.790 --> 00:48:06.690
And she said, I would wear something denim.
她说，我觉得穿件牛仔材质的就行。

1062
00:48:07.510 --> 00:48:08.230
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1063
00:48:09.310 --> 00:48:10.570
What is wrong with this?
这有什么问题吗？

1064
00:48:10.850 --> 00:48:11.910
What did you wear?
你穿了什么？

1065
00:48:12.090 --> 00:48:13.750
She was like, do you have a denim vest?
她说，你有牛仔背心吗？

1066
00:48:13.990 --> 00:48:14.890
No, she didn't.
不，她没说。

1067
00:48:14.950 --> 00:48:16.310
And I was like, I do.
我说，我有。

1068
00:48:16.490 --> 00:48:17.490
I do, actually.
真的，我有。

1069
00:48:17.690 --> 00:48:19.650
She goes, well, denim vest or a denim jacket?
她说，那是牛仔背心还是牛仔外套？

1070
00:48:19.650 --> 00:48:21.310
Well, I didn't have a denim jacket.
好吧，我没有牛仔外套。

1071
00:48:21.570 --> 00:48:23.110
This is peak 90s, guys.
伙计们，这可是90年代的巅峰。

1072
00:48:23.690 --> 00:48:26.690
Then the photographer, I think, just zoomed in.
然后摄影师，我想，他直接拉近了镜头。

1073
00:48:26.830 --> 00:48:28.070
It's like neck up.
就像是只拍脖子以上。

1074
00:48:28.390 --> 00:48:30.010
This is my first head shot.
这是我的第一张头像照。

1075
00:48:30.870 --> 00:48:32.410
Oh, you look cute.
噢，你看起来很可爱。

1076
00:48:33.170 --> 00:48:34.830
And it doesn't look like a veSt.
而且看起来不像背心。

1077
00:48:34.830 --> 00:48:36.110
It looks like a denim shirt.
看起来像件牛仔衬衫。

1078
00:48:36.410 --> 00:48:36.610
Okay.
好吧。

1079
00:48:37.690 --> 00:48:39.210
Then, this is in New York.
然后，这是在纽约拍的。

1080
00:48:39.770 --> 00:48:45.390
Then I move to Los Angeles, and I'm like, they're all like, well, you've got to get a real more
后来我搬到了洛杉矶，他们都说，你得拍一张更专业的

1081
00:48:45.390 --> 00:48:47.350
body head shot, right?
全身头像照，对吧？

1082
00:48:47.350 --> 00:48:47.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1083
00:48:47.590 --> 00:48:48.590
Like, not just your head.
就是说，不只是拍头。

1084
00:48:48.750 --> 00:48:50.310
You need a, like, three-quarter, right?
你需要一张，那种四分之三身位的，对吧？

1085
00:48:50.430 --> 00:48:50.590
Yeah.
没错。

1086
00:48:50.710 --> 00:48:51.310
That was the thing.
那时候流行这个。

1087
00:48:51.370 --> 00:48:52.010
That was the big thing.
那是当时的大热门。

1088
00:48:52.090 --> 00:48:55.350
You were supposed to have, like, a head shot and a three-quarter shot.
你得准备一张头像照和一张四分之三身位照。

1089
00:48:55.590 --> 00:48:55.770
Right.
对。

1090
00:48:56.110 --> 00:48:58.410
So I was like, okay, let's do this again.
