1737
01:13:52.010 --> 01:13:56.230
Dwight is also now going to try to talk Andy out of going.
德怀特现在还要试图劝阻安迪不要离开。

1738
01:13:56.410 --> 01:14:00.030
He says, listen, I have everything to gain by you leaving, but don't go.
他说，听着，你离开对我来说好处多多，但别走。

1739
01:14:00.190 --> 01:14:01.710
Please, I've seen you perform.
求你了，我见过你的表演。

1740
01:14:01.910 --> 01:14:04.090
Dear God, don't quit your day job.
天哪，千万别辞掉你的正职。

1741
01:14:04.330 --> 01:14:09.890
And then Andy has this response, which I just love Ed Helms so much.
然后安迪做出了这个回应，我真的太喜欢艾德·赫尔姆斯了。

1742
01:14:09.990 --> 01:14:10.790
This made me laugh.
这让我笑了出来。

1743
01:14:10.970 --> 01:14:16.350
In a very Cockney accent, he says, nothing is impossible to him who will try.
他用一种非常地道的伦敦腔说：“对于愿意尝试的人来说，没有什么是不可能的。”

1744
01:14:16.850 --> 01:14:19.670
Alex, isn't it great if he were Cockney?
亚历克斯，如果他是伦敦腔，那不是太棒了吗？

1745
01:14:19.830 --> 01:14:23.130
I cannot do a very good Cockney accent, but Ed's is great.
我模仿不好伦敦腔，但艾德模仿得太棒了。

1746
01:14:23.150 --> 01:14:26.990
And I just love that that's how he chose to say that quote.
我特别喜欢他选择用那种方式说出那句名言。

1747
01:14:26.990 --> 01:14:32.070
And then Andy has this talking head where he says, I'm going to make it.
然后安迪有一个采访镜头，他说，我会成功的。

1748
01:14:32.630 --> 01:14:37.690
Every person that has been on Conan has a crazy story about how they made it.
每一个上过柯南秀的人都有一个关于他们如何成功的疯狂故事。

1749
01:14:38.010 --> 01:14:39.290
Every person.
每一个人。

1750
01:14:39.650 --> 01:14:40.070
Yeah.
没错。

1751
01:14:40.510 --> 01:14:44.450
That's because every person who's on Conan made it.
那是因为每一个上过柯南节目的人都成功了。

1752
01:14:45.310 --> 01:14:54.830
You know, I have to say, though, when you try to do something like this, it does serve you to have a little delusion.
不过我得说，当你尝试做这种事时，带点妄想确实对你有帮助。

1753
01:14:55.250 --> 01:15:05.570
I mean, nothing makes you get in your car and drive across the country with your denim vest on and you're ready to take the world.
我是说，如果不是这样，你哪来的动力穿着牛仔背心，开车横跨全国，准备去征服世界呢？

1754
01:15:05.570 --> 01:15:06.470
That's right.
没错。

1755
01:15:06.730 --> 01:15:11.890
I mean, there is there's ambition, but there's a healthy amount of delusion.
我的意思是，人要有野心，但也要有适度的妄想。

1756
01:15:12.730 --> 01:15:14.430
So Andy's not wrong.
所以安迪没说错。

1757
01:15:14.630 --> 01:15:16.810
And you do have to be your own champion.
你确实得成为自己的头号支持者。

1758
01:15:16.810 --> 01:15:20.750
Even when other people don't see it in you, you have to see it in yourself.
即使别人不看好你，你也必须看好自己。

1759
01:15:20.990 --> 01:15:21.470
It's true.
确实如此。

1760
01:15:21.650 --> 01:15:25.010
I thought a lot about my early days watching this episode.
看这一集的时候，我回想了很多早年的经历。

1761
01:15:25.010 --> 01:15:33.470
I remember telling my manager at 1-800-DENTIST that I was going to quit 1-800-DENTIST to focus on my one-woman show.
我记得我曾告诉我在1-800-DENTIST的经理，我要辞职去专注于我的单人秀。

1762
01:15:35.230 --> 01:15:35.790
And?
然后呢？

1763
01:15:36.130 --> 01:15:36.970
I did.
我真的辞了。

1764
01:15:41.050 --> 01:15:42.870
One-woman show full of characters.
那是一场充满各种角色的单人秀。

1765
01:15:43.150 --> 01:15:44.890
It did a whole bunch of characters.
里面演了一大堆角色。

1766
01:15:45.790 --> 01:15:47.010
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

1767
01:15:47.010 --> 01:15:50.450
I remember that I was at a job interview.
我记得当时我正在参加一场面试。

1768
01:15:51.390 --> 01:15:57.070
And in the interview, I wanted to be very honest and upfront about why I was really here.
面试时，我想坦诚直白地说明我来这里的真实目的。

1769
01:15:57.170 --> 01:15:57.390
Sure.
当然。

1770
01:15:57.550 --> 01:16:00.590
And it was not to be part of media sales.
我来这儿可不是为了做媒体销售的。

1771
01:16:01.290 --> 01:16:08.890
And so I said, I do feel like I need to tell you that, you know, I'm really here pursuing an acting career.
所以我说，我觉得有必要告诉你，我其实是为了追求演艺事业才来这儿的。

1772
01:16:08.890 --> 01:16:11.190
So that is going to be my main focus.
所以那会是我的工作重心。

1773
01:16:11.190 --> 01:16:13.290
I'm really here for that.
我来这儿主要是为了那个。

1774
01:16:13.470 --> 01:16:13.610
Yeah.
嗯。

1775
01:16:14.890 --> 01:16:19.450
And the person literally said, I think that'll be fine.
结果那个人竟然说，我觉得没问题。

1776
01:16:20.050 --> 01:16:22.710
If it becomes a problem, we'll deal with it.
如果以后成了问题，我们再处理。

1777
01:16:22.930 --> 01:16:23.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1778
01:16:23.270 --> 01:16:27.910
Like, sort of like, okay, we'll see you tomorrow at 9.
就好像是说，好吧，明天早上九点见。

1779
01:16:28.570 --> 01:16:30.430
Don't think I'm going to have to worry.
别以为我会为此担心。

1780
01:16:30.650 --> 01:16:34.450
Well, my manager at 1-800-DENTIST said, anytime you want to come back.
我在1-800-DENTIST的经理倒是说，随时欢迎我回去。

1781
01:16:34.750 --> 01:16:35.090
No.
不。

1782
01:16:35.390 --> 01:16:36.350
You're welcome.
不客气。

1783
01:16:38.470 --> 01:16:39.590
I was like, okay.
我当时心想，好吧。

1784
01:16:39.590 --> 01:16:44.370
And I remember, like, driving in my car, leaving there, being like, I'm never going to go back.
我记得开车离开时，心里想着，我再也不会回去了。

1785
01:16:44.750 --> 01:16:45.730
You'll see.
走着瞧吧。

1786
01:16:46.050 --> 01:16:49.990
My one-woman show is going to be the talk of the town.
我的单人秀一定会成为全城热议的话题。

1787
01:16:50.170 --> 01:16:51.350
All my characters.
我所有的角色都会火。

1788
01:16:52.110 --> 01:16:53.150
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1789
01:16:53.910 --> 01:16:59.130
Well, most people didn't maybe totally support our delusions.
好吧，大多数人可能并不完全支持我们的妄想。

1790
01:16:59.510 --> 01:17:01.610
Erin certainly does not support Andy's.
艾琳肯定不支持安迪的妄想。

1791
01:17:01.730 --> 01:17:04.030
Well, Andy says, I'm going to ask you.
安迪说，我要问问你。

1792
01:17:04.150 --> 01:17:05.510
You're honest Erin, right?
你是诚实的艾琳，对吧？

1793
01:17:06.150 --> 01:17:07.510
Erin cannot tell a lie.
艾琳从不说谎。

1794
01:17:07.670 --> 01:17:07.890
Yeah.
嗯。

1795
01:17:07.890 --> 01:17:12.670
And she says, pretty bluntly, that she's worried that he might become homeless or even starve.
她非常直白地说，她担心他可能会流落街头甚至饿死。

1796
01:17:13.190 --> 01:17:13.390
Yeah.
是啊。

1797
01:17:13.870 --> 01:17:16.830
And this is going to finally take the wind out of Andy's sails.
这终于让安迪泄了气。

1798
01:17:17.070 --> 01:17:17.410
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1799
01:17:17.930 --> 01:17:19.750
Andy walks into the conference room.
安迪走进会议室。

1800
01:17:19.950 --> 01:17:23.090
And before he could even say anything, David says, you know what?
他还没来得及开口，大卫就说，你知道吗？

1801
01:17:23.090 --> 01:17:24.470
You can stay on as a salesman.
你可以继续担任销售员。

1802
01:17:25.150 --> 01:17:25.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1803
01:17:26.030 --> 01:17:27.290
And I'm sad for Andy.
而且我为安迪感到难过。

1804
01:17:27.510 --> 01:17:29.950
He was so excited at the beginning of this episode.
他在这一集刚开始的时候那么兴奋。

1805
01:17:30.190 --> 01:17:31.190
Well, don't worry.
嗯，别担心。

1806
01:17:31.330 --> 01:17:31.850
I know.
我知道。

1807
01:17:32.430 --> 01:17:33.670
There's part two coming.
还有第二部分呢。

1808
01:17:33.870 --> 01:17:34.850
Part two is coming.
第二部分马上就来。

1809
01:17:35.090 --> 01:17:36.630
We're going to end on a big cliffhanger.
我们要以一个巨大的悬念结束。

1810
01:17:37.270 --> 01:17:40.550
David Wallace is going to call Dwight into the conference room.
大卫·华莱士要把德怀特叫进会议室了。

1811
01:17:41.390 --> 01:17:42.430
Dun-dun-dun.
当当当。

1812
01:17:42.550 --> 01:17:43.270
Dun-dun-dun.
当当当。

1813
01:17:43.330 --> 01:17:44.010
To be continued.
未完待续。

1814
01:17:44.330 --> 01:17:44.670
Yes.
没错。

1815
01:17:44.670 --> 01:17:51.250
We did get a fan catch for this very final moment of Dwight shutting the door behind him.
我们确实收到了一位粉丝关于德怀特关上身后房门这一最后时刻的发现。

1816
01:17:51.730 --> 01:17:53.130
It's from Xenia W.
来自不列颠哥伦比亚省的Xenia W.

1817
01:17:53.890 --> 01:17:56.530
in British Columbia and also Summer P.
以及密苏里州圣查尔斯的Summer P.

1818
01:17:56.790 --> 01:17:58.030
from St. Charles, Missouri.
她们为我们提供了这一集最后一个镜头里的“妈妈侦探”时刻。

1819
01:17:58.350 --> 01:18:02.710
They have a mom detectives moment for us in this very final shot of this episode.
是什么？

1820
01:18:02.990 --> 01:18:03.550
What is it?
我这就告诉你。

1821
01:18:03.790 --> 01:18:04.830
I'm going to tell you.
我还要提前告诉你，这个谜题同样会悬而未决。

1822
01:18:04.830 --> 01:18:08.810
I'm also going to tell you ahead of time, this one is going to go unsolved as well.
哦。

1823
01:18:09.150 --> 01:18:09.330
Oh.
好吧。

1824
01:18:09.670 --> 01:18:09.910
Okay.
所以没什么新鲜的。

1825
01:18:10.030 --> 01:18:10.770
So nothing new.
没错。

1826
01:18:11.130 --> 01:18:11.390
Correct.
在20分58秒时，当德怀特关上会议室的门去和大卫·华莱士谈话时，

1827
01:18:12.510 --> 01:18:18.250
At 20 minutes and 58 seconds, as Dwight closes the conference room door to talk to David Wallace,
德怀特头后的墙上有一滴不明液体留下的痕迹。

1828
01:18:18.590 --> 01:18:23.630
there is a single trailing drip of something on the wall behind Dwight's head.
咦。

1829
01:18:23.750 --> 01:18:24.010
Ew.
她们看不出那是什么，这让她们抓狂。

1830
01:18:24.490 --> 01:18:27.470
They can't tell what it is, and it's driving them crazy.
她们想知道，那是咖啡吗？

1831
01:18:27.730 --> 01:18:29.470
They want to know, is it coffee?
是巧克力酱吗？

1832
01:18:29.690 --> 01:18:31.190
Is it chocolate sauce?
是删减片段的一部分吗？

1833
01:18:31.450 --> 01:18:33.390
Is it part of a deleted scene?
是在人头高度吗？

1834
01:18:33.390 --> 01:18:35.170
Is it head high?
差不多，是的。

1835
01:18:36.110 --> 01:18:38.410
It's about, yeah, it is.
嗯哼。

1836
01:18:38.730 --> 01:18:38.990
Mm-hmm.
哈。

1837
01:18:39.110 --> 01:18:39.290
Huh.
会不会是剧组成员不小心溅上去的，而没人发现？

1838
01:18:39.790 --> 01:18:43.410
Was it perhaps splattered there from a crew member and no one caught it?
珍娜，安吉拉，妈妈侦探们能解开这个谜吗？

1839
01:18:43.770 --> 01:18:47.290
Jenna, Angela, can the mom detectives solve this?
我会回去重看一遍。

1840
01:18:47.510 --> 01:18:49.390
I will go back and re-watch it.
我会把它放大看看。

1841
01:18:49.630 --> 01:18:50.750
I'll zoom in on it.
我看过了。

1842
01:18:50.810 --> 01:18:51.590
I looked at it.
我有它的照片。

1843
01:18:51.670 --> 01:18:52.610
I have a picture of it.
哦，让我们看看。

1844
01:18:52.710 --> 01:18:53.570
Oh, let's see it.
看看能不能帮到你。

1845
01:18:53.690 --> 01:18:54.650
See if it'll help you.
好的。

1846
01:18:54.890 --> 01:18:55.170
Okay.
我差点就在上面画了个圈。

1847
01:18:55.670 --> 01:18:57.690
I almost drew a circle around it.
哦。

1848
01:18:57.930 --> 01:18:58.290
Oh.
我觉得看起来像马克笔痕迹。

1849
01:18:59.990 --> 01:19:01.930
I think it looks like Sharpie.
马克笔。

1850
01:19:01.930 --> 01:19:01.980
Sharpie.
马克笔。

1851
01:19:02.750 --> 01:19:04.090
No, it looks like a drip.
不，看起来像滴落的痕迹。

1852
01:19:04.490 --> 01:19:04.870
No.
不。

1853
01:19:05.150 --> 01:19:06.290
There's a drip at the bottom.
底部有个滴落的痕迹。

1854
01:19:06.530 --> 01:19:07.130
Look at it.
你看。

1855
01:19:07.230 --> 01:19:08.510
There's a little bubble of drip.
有个小小的滴落气泡。

1856
01:19:08.770 --> 01:19:10.810
Where the ink, like, makes the bigger dot.
就是墨水形成大圆点的地方。

1857
01:19:11.030 --> 01:19:12.930
Why would someone draw Sharpie on the wall?
为什么会有人在墙上用记号笔乱画？

1858
01:19:12.930 --> 01:19:13.970
I don't think they meant to.
我觉得他们不是故意的。

1859
01:19:14.930 --> 01:19:16.250
I don't think it's Sharpie.
我觉得那不是记号笔。

1860
01:19:16.610 --> 01:19:17.930
I want to look at it again.
我想再看一遍。

1861
01:19:18.390 --> 01:19:20.050
It looks like black Sharpie to me.
在我看来那就是黑色记号笔。

1862
01:19:20.970 --> 01:19:23.070
Oh, when you really zoom in on it.
哦，当你真的放大看的时候。

1863
01:19:23.230 --> 01:19:23.570
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1864
01:19:23.850 --> 01:19:25.430
I see what you're doing there.
我明白你在做什么了。

1865
01:19:26.370 --> 01:19:26.850
Okay.
好吧。

1866
01:19:27.110 --> 01:19:27.450
Well.
嗯。

1867
01:19:28.310 --> 01:19:29.930
My theory is it's Sharpie.
我的理论是那就是记号笔。

1868
01:19:30.110 --> 01:19:34.850
Xenia, Summer, when you zoom in on it, I don't know.
Xenia，Summer，当你放大看的时候，我不知道。

1869
01:19:34.990 --> 01:19:36.770
What if when it's a video, it's moving?
如果它是视频，它会动吗？

1870
01:19:37.950 --> 01:19:40.650
I'm going to have to re-watch it to be continued.
我得重看一遍，未完待续。

1871
01:19:41.430 --> 01:19:43.550
To be continued, just like this episode.
未完待续，就像这一集一样。

1872
01:19:43.630 --> 01:19:44.550
Just like this episode.
就像这一集一样。

1873
01:19:44.550 --> 01:19:48.630
I do want to give a shout out to the writer of this episode, Nikki Schwartz Wright.
我确实想向这一集的编剧Nikki Schwartz Wright致敬。

1874
01:19:49.130 --> 01:19:50.050
She's fantastic.
她太棒了。

1875
01:19:50.050 --> 01:19:51.370
We traded texts.
我们互发了短信。

1876
01:19:51.630 --> 01:19:58.190
And I told her how special this episode is to me because I loved, loved getting to see
我告诉她这一集对我来说有多特别，因为我非常、非常喜欢看到

1877
01:19:58.190 --> 01:20:00.090
the range of emotion in Angela Martin.
Angela Martin的情感起伏。

1878
01:20:00.710 --> 01:20:03.050
A lot happens for her in this episode.
这一集里她经历了很多。

1879
01:20:03.050 --> 01:20:04.750
And it had to build and grow.
而且这种情绪需要铺垫和递进。

1880
01:20:04.890 --> 01:20:06.610
And I thought Nikki wrote it so well.
我觉得Nikki写得非常好。

1881
01:20:06.810 --> 01:20:11.830
And she wrote me back and said that she has bronchitis or she would have left us a voice
她回信说她得了支气管炎，否则她会给我们留一条语音

1882
01:20:11.830 --> 01:20:12.130
memo.
备忘录的。

1883
01:20:12.310 --> 01:20:12.630
Aw.
啊。

1884
01:20:13.130 --> 01:20:18.290
But in the text, she praised our writer's room and said they truly wrote these episodes
但在短信里，她称赞了我们的编剧团队，说这些剧集确实是他们

1885
01:20:18.290 --> 01:20:18.890
as a group.
集体创作的。

1886
01:20:18.890 --> 01:20:21.030
And she didn't want to take any of the credit.
她不想独占功劳。

1887
01:20:21.530 --> 01:20:22.390
I know.
我知道。

1888
01:20:22.970 --> 01:20:23.750
So sweet.
太贴心了。

1889
01:20:23.970 --> 01:20:26.190
She was really happy that they brought me joy.
她很高兴这些内容能给我带来快乐。

1890
01:20:26.910 --> 01:20:29.590
And she's just so talented in a class act.
她真的非常有才华，而且很有风度。

1891
01:20:29.730 --> 01:20:31.930
And I just wanted to say, Nikki, I hope you feel better.
我只是想说，Nikki，希望你早日康复。

1892
01:20:32.090 --> 01:20:35.290
And thanks for giving Angela Martin such a great episode.
谢谢你给了Angela Martin这么棒的一集。

1893
01:20:35.550 --> 01:20:39.270
And it's really just going to get even better, too, in the second half.
而且在下半部分，情况还会变得更好。

1894
01:20:39.270 --> 01:20:41.590
In terms of that Angela Martin emotion.
就Angela Martin的情感而言。

1895
01:20:41.910 --> 01:20:43.570
Oh, some big stuff is coming.
哦，大事要发生了。

1896
01:20:44.350 --> 01:20:45.210
I cried.
我哭了。

1897
01:20:45.270 --> 01:20:46.690
We'll talk about it next week.
我们下周再聊这个。

1898
01:20:46.890 --> 01:20:47.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1899
01:20:47.770 --> 01:20:50.970
Well, I want to give a big thank you again to Michael Imperioli.
嗯，我想再次向Michael Imperioli表示衷心的感谢。

1900
01:20:51.250 --> 01:20:54.830
